JSON vs JSONL

| Feature        | JSON                       | JSONL                               |
| -------------- | -------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |
| Full form      | JavaScript Object Notation | JSON Lines                          |
| Structure      | One complete JSON document | One JSON object per line            |
| Best for       | Small/structured data      | Large datasets and AI training data |
| File extension | `.json`                    | `.jsonl`                            |
| Example        | One big object/array       | Many separate JSON records          |


===========

Simple visual example

JSON:

[
  {
    "question": "How to increase bakery sales?",
    "answer": "Use social media marketing."
  },
  {
    "question": "How to reduce food waste?",
    "answer": "Analyze daily sales."
  }
]

==========

JSONL:

{"question":"How to increase bakery sales?","answer":"Use social media marketing."}
{"question":"How to reduce food waste?","answer":"Analyze daily sales."}

========

Easy memory trick 🧠
JSON  = One complete data document

JSONL = JSON
        JSON
        JSON
        Each JSON on a separate Line

==========

Gemma 2 fine-tuning, JSONL is commonly useful because each line can represent one training example.

